meta {
  name: Bulk approve
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/bills/bulk/approve
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "ids": ["{{billId}}"]
  }
}

docs {
  Admin or Approver. Approves every supplied bill independently (each
  in its own transaction). Try mixing a PENDING_APPROVAL id with a
  DRAFT id — the draft fails with BILL_INVALID_TRANSITION while the
  pending one is approved. Viewer -> 403.

  Response shape (every bulk endpoint):
      { results: [{ id, ok: true, data: <entity> } |
                  { id, ok: false, error: { code, message } }],
        summary: { total, succeeded, failed } }
  HTTP status is always 200 — partial failure is the common case.
  Empty or duplicate `ids` -> 400 BULK_INVALID_IDS.
}
